@startuml 03-sequence-voice-intake
title Voice Intake (AI Assistant) — Extraction &amp; Safety Gate (Sequence Diagram)

actor Customer
actor "Office Admin" as Admin
participant "Browser UI\n(public/app.js)" as UI
participant "HTTP Server\n(server/index.js)" as API
participant "Store\n(server/store.js)" as Store
participant "Classifier (stub)\n(server/classifier.js)" as Classifier

Customer -> Admin: Describes the fault over the phone
Admin -> UI: Speaks near mic (Web Speech API)\nor types the transcript
UI -> UI: Live transcription fills the\ntranscript field
Admin -> UI: Click "Extract details"
UI -> API: POST /api/voice-intake {transcript}
API -> Store: listSites()
Store --> API: sites[]
API -> Classifier: classifyIntake(transcript, sites)
Classifier -> Classifier: match fault-type patterns\n(regex, confidence-scored)
Classifier -> Classifier: match candidate site\n(phone number / name / address words)
Classifier -> Classifier: detect safety flags\n(gas smell / CO alarm phrases)
Classifier --> API: {faultType, errorCode, site,\nsafetyFlags, requiresHumanReview}
API --> UI: 200 draft
UI --> Admin: Show draft with confidence scores

alt safety flag detected
  UI --> Admin: BLOCKED — handle as an\nemergency call, action disabled
else confident fault type + matched site
  Admin -> UI: Click "Review in guided form"
  UI -> UI: Pre-fill guided form\n(site, fault type, error code, transcript)
  note right: continues as the Guided Web Form\nsequence (see 02-sequence-guided-web-form)
else low confidence or no site match
  UI --> Admin: Flagged "needs human review",\nnothing pre-filled automatically
end

@enduml
